    "question": "How many Cybertrucks did Tesla deliver in each month of the last quarter?",
    "answer": "The provided SEC filing evidence does not contain monthly Cybertruck delivery figures. Tesla's operational summaries in its quarterly press releases report deliveries on a quarterly basis, organized into two categories: \"Model 3/Y deliveries\" and \"Other models deliveries\" [c1, c2, c3, c4]. Cybertruck is listed separately in the vehicle capacity tables with an installed annual capacity of >125,000 and a production status, but no delivery count is provided for Cybertruck in any of the excerpts [c1, c2, c3, c4, c5]. For example, the Q1 2025 press release shows \"Other models deliveries\" of 12,881 for the quarter and the Q3 2025 press release shows \"Other models deliveries\" of 15,933 for the quarter, but neither provides a Cybertruck-specific delivery figure or a monthly breakdown [c3, c4]. None of the provided excerpts contain any monthly delivery data for any vehicle model. Therefore, the number of Cybertrucks delivered in each month of the last quarter cannot be determined from the provided evidence.",
